# Go sources and module files are LF in the repo and in the working tree -
# gofmt/go tooling is LF-sensitive, and core.autocrlf=true would otherwise
# re-check them out as CRLF on Windows and fail the wg-go gate (BI-PF-0412 RCCA).
*.go text eol=lf
go.mod text eol=lf
go.sum text eol=lf

# Backlog shared stores (BI-PF-1176): never text-merge.
# - append-only history records: built-in union keeps both sides' lines.
**/backlog/history/*.jsonl merge=union
# - work ITEM records are SOURCE: never let a stale side win a merge. pf-item keeps the
#   NEWEST version per item (max revision, then updated_at) - see RCCA (state-sync clobber).
**/backlog/items/*.json merge=pf-item
# - DERIVED lean indexes: regenerate from items/ via the pf-derived merge driver (install_hooks.py).
**/backlog/open.json merge=pf-derived
**/backlog/closed.json merge=pf-derived
# - shared label/id counters: max-merge from the three merge inputs (BI-PF-1290, step 3).
**/backlog/counters.json merge=pf-derived
# - DERIVED generated docs: regenerate from the backlog on merge (BI-PF-1290).
product-forge/docs/BACKLOG-SUMMARY.md merge=pf-derived
product-forge/docs/documentation-index.html merge=pf-derived
